  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1209 AM CDT Sun Jul 19 2026\n\nDry pattern still looks to return for much of the upcoming week. \nThe upper level ridge will shift a little farther south and build \ninto West Central Texas. Temperatures will climb back to near or a\nlittle above seasonal normals, with the hottest readings across \nthe northern portions of the area closest to the center of the \nridge. Afternoon highs approaching or exceeding the 100 degree \nmark look possible once again. \n\nWill watch the tropical system in the Gulf, which a few of the\nmodels have drifting west this week. Even with that said, those\nsame models don't show much in the way of any precipitation \nchances so a dry forecast looks likely even then.",
